rows='';last=None
for group,title,kind,decision,fit,status,url,demo in catalogue:
 if group!=last:
  if last:rows+='</tbody></table></div></section>'
  rows+=f'<section><h2>{html.escape(group)}</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Use case / decision</th><th>Typed question</th><th>Why a bounded model might fit</th><th>Evidence / experiment</th></tr></thead><tbody>';last=group
 link=(f'<a href="{url}">Source</a>. ' if url else '')
 if demo:link+=f'<a href="'+('adaptation.html' if demo=='adaptation' else 'lab.html?demo='+demo)+'">Try the pattern</a>'
 else:link+='Catalogue only: a separate integration or domain evaluation would teach more than a duplicate generic demo.'
 rows+=f'<tr><td><strong>{html.escape(title)}</strong><p>{html.escape(decision)}</p></td><td>{kind}</td><td>{html.escape(fit)}</td><td>{html.escape(status)}<p>{link}</p></td></tr>'
rows+='</tbody></table></div></section>'
page('decision-models/catalogue.html','The use-case catalogue','''<h1>What could you<br>build with this?</h1><p class="lead">A catalogue before a codebase: 37 places a bounded decision might belong, from documented demos to deliberately speculative experiments.</p><p>Read a row as <strong>decision → primitive → reason to try it</strong>, not “AI is always better”. Rules, classical classifiers or a generative model may win. Business process is an additional lens, not a stronger evidence grade.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="lab.html">Explore eight working patterns</a><a href="lab.html#generator">Generate another experiment</a><a href="./">Read the mechanism and evidence</a></div><p class="notice">The eight local interactions work with explicitly synthetic decisions; actual Jev needs a key and actual Kev needs a local server. The unfamiliar-label pair and architecture calculator add two more experiments. None of the illustrative numbers is a model measurement.</p>'''+rows+'''<h2>From catalogue to experiments</h2><p>One shell deliberately supports many patterns: tool selection, agent routing, adaptive UI, moderation, scoring, evidence ranking, state-machine transitions and game moves. Each exposes state, question schema, distribution and threshold. The adaptation page adds a two-arm context experiment; the architecture page makes the cost assumptions editable.</p><p>For more breadth, use the generator to create a schema—not arbitrary executable code. A new label task earns a new specification; a new interaction or domain-specific evaluation earns actual implementation work. That distinction prevents a long list of differently titled copies masquerading as a demo suite.</p>''')
